$test['Pets'] = 'A senior Golden Retriever looks directly toward the viewer in soft Black and Grey Realism. The grey muzzle slightly cloudy eyes and uneven fur around the ears are preserved rather than beautified away. The portrait fades naturally into skin below the chest so nothing feels like a photograph pasted onto the body'
$cats['Pets']['Pets This Is My Pet'] = @('A senior Golden Retriever looks directly toward the viewer in soft Black and Grey Realism. The grey muzzle slightly cloudy eyes and uneven fur around the ears are preserved rather than beautified away. The portrait fades naturally into skin below the chest so nothing feels like a photograph pasted onto the body','A black cat is shown almost entirely through darkness. Most of the body disappears into a controlled Blackwork field while green eyes whiskers and a few highlights reveal the individual face','A French Bulldog is captured from slightly below with its familiar oversized ears and intensely serious expression. Rich Colour Realism preserves the pets exact coat pattern while deep burgundy shadow creates a sophisticated portrait rather than a cute illustration','A chestnut horse turns its head toward the wearer. The eye muzzle and individual blaze marking receive realistic detail while the mane breaks into loose Sketch strokes that follow the shoulder','An orange tabby sits in the exact hunched position it always takes before jumping. Illustrative linework captures the stripe pattern and expression while selected warm orange color identifies the actual cat','A three-legged mixed-breed dog stands proudly rather than hiding the missing limb. The design uses restrained Black and Grey Realism with a full-body silhouette so the physical difference becomes part of the animals identity','An African grey parrot turns toward the viewer with extraordinary feather texture and a sharp intelligent eye. Most feathers remain black and grey while the natural red tail becomes the only saturated color','A tiny Chihuahua is portrayed at unexpectedly grand scale with a dignified expression and enormous alert ears. Fine Black and Grey Realism treats the little animal with the visual seriousness normally reserved for a large portrait','A lop-eared rabbit rests with one ear folded differently from the other. Fine Line and delicate Dotwork preserve the softness of the fur without turning the animal into a generic rabbit illustration','A Doberman faces forward with one naturally imperfect ear sitting differently from the other. Deep black areas merge into negative skin while the eyes and muzzle are carefully resolved')
$cats['Pets']['Pets Portrait Ten Different Ways'] = @('A Bernese Mountain Dog is rendered in full Colour Realism with the exact rust white and black facial markings preserved. Snow reflected subtly in the lower fur gives the portrait atmosphere without creating a rectangular landscape','A Siamese cat becomes a Fine Line portrait made almost entirely from selective contours. The dark mask ears and blue eyes provide just enough identifying information while much of the white face remains natural skin','A Greyhound is drawn in Sketch style with several searching contours around the long muzzle and ears. One eye and the final profile resolve confidently while earlier drawing attempts remain visible','A Pomeranian is transformed through Watercolour rather than simply painted brightly. The fluffy coat dissolves into wet orange gold and soft crimson washes while the eyes and nose remain precisely recognizable','A Pit Bull portrait uses contemporary Blackwork. One side of the face becomes a large solid black shape while carefully designed negative skin reveals the forehead eye and distinctive muzzle','A Sphynx cat is treated as an elegant Dotwork study. Thousands of controlled points describe wrinkles ears and facial planes while untouched skin becomes the highlights','A German Shepherd becomes a Neo-Traditional portrait with strong silhouette rich black deep rust muted gold and emerald accents. The individual ear shape and facial markings remain faithful to the real pet','A cockatiel is rendered as a tiny Micro Realism portrait perched naturally rather than as a floating head. The yellow crest and orange cheek remain vivid while the rest stays delicately realistic','A Bearded Dragon is rendered through Colour Realism with extraordinary attention to scale texture and the animals actual expression. Warm amber light makes the skin dimensional without inventing fantasy coloring','A scruffy mixed-breed rescue becomes an Illustrative portrait with visible ink drawing loose fur marks and selective brown color. The asymmetrical ears and unruly coat are deliberately preserved')
$cats['Pets']['Pets The Little Things That Make Them Them'] = @('A Labrador carries the same battered tennis ball it has carried for years. The portrait is secondary to the relationship between the dogs familiar expression and the destroyed object with every tear and tooth mark preserved','A tuxedo cat is curled into its exact sleeping position with one paw covering its face. Fine Line drawing and small areas of black preserve the distinctive white paws and chest','A Dachshund stands with the specific stuffed toy it refuses to give up. Rather than making the scene comedic soft Illustrative treatment turns an ordinary daily ritual into an intimate portrait','A Husky looks through the partially open window of a car with wind pushing the fur backward. The dogs face is the hero while the window edge provides just enough context to capture a favorite behavior','A Maine Coon stretches with both front paws extended and its enormous tail rising behind it. The composition celebrates the pets actual posture rather than relying on a standard face portrait','A rescue dog with one damaged eye is shown in three-quarter portrait. The scar and closed eye remain exactly as they are while Colour Realism gives extraordinary attention to the healthy eye','A green-cheek conure perches on the persons finger leaning forward in the exact curious posture familiar to its owner. Bright natural color is concentrated on the bird while the hand remains Fine Line','A senior Poodle rests its chin on its favorite blanket. Soft Black and Grey Realism preserves the ageing eyes curled fur and worn texture of the blanket','A pet rat stands upright holding a tiny piece of food between its actual delicate hands. Detailed Illustrative drawing treats the animal seriously and beautifully emphasizing whiskers paws and intelligent eyes','A horse presses its forehead against its persons forehead. Only the human profile and horses head are needed with the contact point becoming the center of the composition')
$cats['Pets']['Pets Paws Noses Tags and Real Marks'] = @('A dogs actual paw print is reproduced exactly preserving uneven pads and imperfections. Inside the largest pad sits a tiny Micro Realism portrait of the same Border Collie','A cats actual nose print is enlarged into a Dotwork texture field. From normal viewing distance the texture resolves into the silhouette of the black-and-white cat itself','A worn metal dog tag is rendered in extraordinary Colour Realism. Instead of displaying the pet directly the curved chrome surface contains a subtle reflection of the Boxer that wore it','A rabbits actual paw impressions form a quiet path that leads toward a delicate Fine Line portrait at the end. The spacing follows the animals real hopping rhythm rather than generic decorative paw icons','A German Shepherds worn leather collar curves naturally around the upper arm. Its scratches buckle and tag are reproduced faithfully while the dogs eyes appear subtly within the deepest shadow','The actual paw print of a Great Dane becomes a bold Negative Space composition. Dense black surrounds the irregular print while a Fine Line profile of the dog crosses partially through it','A Siamese cats small bell and worn collar are rendered as an Ornamental keepsake. The actual collar shape remains recognizable while elegant linework radiates outward without overwhelming the personal object','A horses actual horseshoe is recreated with its real wear scratches and uneven edges rather than a perfect symbolic horseshoe. A tiny realistic eye of the horse appears reflected in the metal','A parrots shed feather is reproduced at life size with the birds real color pattern. Near the base a tiny Fine Line silhouette of the parrot sits almost hidden','A senior mixed-breed dogs actual nose texture is transformed into a large abstract Dotwork field that gradually resolves into the animals face as the viewer steps back')
$cats['Pets']['Pets Life Together'] = @('A Labrador and its person walk away together down their usual beach shown from behind. The scene is stripped to the two recognizable silhouettes footprints and a thin horizon rather than becoming a full landscape painting','An orange tabby lies across the persons chest with its face tucked under the chin. Fine Line drawing focuses on the intertwined shapes of human arms and cat rather than a formal portrait','A Border Collie runs ahead on a familiar mountain trail and looks back over its shoulder. Colour Realism resolves the dog while the trail and environment loosen into painterly marks','A horse and rider are shown only through the moment after a ride when the rider rests a hand against the horses neck. Sketch and soft Black and Grey emphasize touch rather than sport','A small Terrier sits in the passenger seat looking through the windshield. The composition captures the familiar outline of ears dashboard and road ahead without turning into a novelty scene','A Sphynx cat sleeps against the persons hand with its head fitting naturally into the palm. Fine Line and Dotwork make the wrinkles fingers and contact between them the artwork','A Cockatoo sits on the persons shoulder with its crest relaxed. Only enough of the persons profile is included to show the relationship while the bird receives vivid Colour Realism','A Greyhound and its person run together. Sketch movement creates several faint leg positions around both figures while the final bodies resolve in confident black','A rabbit sits beneath the persons chair exactly where it always waits. Illustrative linework turns the familiar domestic arrangement into a quiet composition about companionship','A senior dog rests its head on the persons knee while a hand lies across the grey muzzle. Black and Grey Realism focuses entirely on touch age and trust')
$cats['Pets']['Pets More Than One'] = @('A Golden Retriever black Labrador and small mixed-breed dog lie together exactly as they normally sleep bodies overlapping naturally rather than appearing as three separate portraits','Two cats touch noses one black and one white. The design uses Negative Space so each animal partially defines the silhouette of the other','Three dogs run toward the viewer at different distances creating natural depth and individual personality rather than a stacked portrait arrangement','A horse and barn cat stand together at the stable door. The enormous difference in scale becomes the visual idea while restrained Illustrative treatment keeps the scene sophisticated','Two French Bulldogs are portrayed back to back each looking in the direction that matches its real personality. Neo-Traditional color distinguishes their markings while one unified silhouette keeps them together','A parrot and small dog share the same composition through the chair where they both normally sit. The environment connects them rather than forcing two unrelated portraits together','Four cats appear as overlapping sleeping shapes in a circular composition. Their individual coat patterns identify each animal while the entire group reads as one soft organic form','Two rescued Pit Bulls stand shoulder to shoulder. Strong Blackwork shapes distinguish each head while scars ears and facial differences preserve their individuality','A dog that has passed and a younger dog that arrived later walk together in the same direction. One is fully resolved while the earlier dog becomes increasingly light and atmospheric without resorting to wings or halos','A rabbit guinea pig and rat form an elegant triangular composition connected by the blanket they shared. Fine Line and soft Dotwork make each animal individually recognizable')
$cats['Pets']['Pets Horses Birds and Other Companions'] = @('A black horse gallops with the mane dissolving into enormous Blackwork brush shapes while the face and distinctive white star remain realistic','A blue-and-gold macaw opens its wings across the shoulder. Colour Realism preserves the individual feather pattern while the composition follows the anatomy rather than presenting the bird frontally','A pet Ball Python wraps naturally around the forearm. Its exact morph pattern is reproduced in Colour Realism so the tattoo represents the individual snake rather than a generic serpent','A Holland Lop rabbit is portrayed through soft Watercolour with one eye and the distinctive ears remaining sharply recognizable while the fur dissolves into muted lavender and warm brown','A Leopard Gecko rests across a branch rendered in Fine Line while selective yellow and orange reproduce the animals real markings','A cockatiel is shown mid-whistle with its crest raised. Sketch lines capture the movement of the head while small natural yellow and orange accents preserve identity','A pet Koi is rendered from above in Colour Realism preserving its exact red white and black pattern. Ripples become subtle Geometric rings that follow the body placement','A pet ferret curves naturally around the upper arm in Illustrative linework. The long anatomy becomes the composition instead of forcing the animal into a conventional portrait','A guinea pig portrait uses Micro Realism with the exact irregular hair direction and facial patch preserved. A tiny favorite piece of bedding appears beneath the paws','A jumping spider is rendered at enlarged scale with extraordinary Micro Realism preserving the pets individual coloration and iridescent chelicerae while maintaining the animals natural beauty')
$cats['Pets']['Pets Memorial Without The Cliches'] = @('A deceased Chocolate Labrador is shown asleep rather than posed for a portrait. The familiar sleeping shape fades softly at the edges while the actual worn collar rests beside the head','A senior cats exact silhouette sits in its favorite window. Only the cat windowsill and a narrow area of evening light remain capturing a daily memory rather than symbolizing death','A deceased horse is remembered through the owners favorite view of its eye and forehead. The real blaze marking and several strands of mane provide all the identity needed','A dogs actual worn tennis ball is rendered in Colour Realism with every tear and puncture visible. A subtle reflection in the rubber surface contains the dogs face','A cats empty collar forms an incomplete circle. Within the open space sits a delicate Fine Line outline of the cats familiar profile using absence itself as part of the memorial','A deceased parrot is represented by one actual feather pattern transitioning gradually into the bird in flight. No halo dates or religious symbols are required','A Boxer with a heavily greyed muzzle looks directly forward. Black and Grey Realism celebrates the animal at the end of its life rather than recreating it as young','A rabbits favorite blanket is shown with the slight body-shaped depression where it always slept. A faint Fine Line contour of the rabbit occupies that space without becoming ghost imagery','Two paw prints use the actual final prints of a beloved dog. Between them runs one understated line based on the route of the walk the owner and dog took every day','A deceased cat is shown walking away through tall grass with its distinctive tail and coat pattern still recognizable. The animal gradually becomes Dotwork atmosphere rather than receiving wings or a halo')
$cats['Pets']['Pets Turn My Pet Into Art'] = @('A Doberman portrait begins in precise Black and Grey Realism around the eyes and muzzle then progressively becomes aggressive black brushwork around the neck and ears. The actual dog remains unmistakable while the portrait becomes contemporary art','A white Persian cat is transformed into an Ornamental composition where elegant jewelry-like lines grow from the natural flow of the fur. The face remains realistic while amethyst-colored accents appear only in the ornamental structure','A Border Collie running at full speed is interpreted through Sketch. Several faint earlier positions of the legs remain visible while the final face and body markings resolve sharply','An orange tabby portrait uses stained-glass structure without losing the animals identity. The real stripe pattern determines the divisions while amber burnt orange and deep teal glass-like fields create the artwork','A Great Dane becomes a monumental Fine Line composition. The enormous dogs full standing silhouette is reduced to beautifully controlled continuous contours with only the eyes and distinctive chest marking developed further','A Miniature Schnauzer is rendered through Dotwork with the characteristic eyebrows and beard emerging from changes in dot density. One eye receives a tiny warm brown accent','A black rabbit becomes a Negative Space tattoo. Deep black botanical forms surround the animal while the rabbit itself is primarily untouched skin with only the eye and selected fur edges defined','A Green Iguana is transformed through Geometric Realism. The head remains realistic while scale patterns progressively reorganize into controlled polygons that follow the arm','A Poodle becomes a sophisticated New School portrait where the characteristic curls are exaggerated into sculptural dimensional forms while the actual face coloring and expression remain recognizable','A chestnut horse is treated through Watercolour and Fine Line. Precise linework establishes the eye and profile while mane and movement become sweeping burnt orange burgundy and indigo washes')
$cats['Pets']['Pets Push Pets'] = @('A senior mixed-breed rescue is portrayed at three stages of life without creating three separate portraits. The puppy emerges lightly through Sketch construction the adult dog resolves through Colour Realism and the grey-muzzled senior becomes the strongest final image. All three positions share the same eyes so the composition reads as one life rather than a timeline graphic','A black cat occupies the center of a large dark composition but is initially almost invisible. Dense Blackwork botanicals night shapes and shadow surround the animal until two luminous eyes reveal that the negative space itself has been forming the cat all along','A Dobermans actual metal tag becomes the center of a hyperrealistic composition. The tag is enormously enlarged and reflects three different memories of the dog across its curved surface: running resting and looking directly at the owner. The dog never appears outside the reflection','Three cats are portrayed not through three faces but through the single bed where they always slept together. Their bodies overlap naturally in different directions each identified through exact coat markings. Morning light creates one unified Colour Realism composition','A horse and rider are shown from behind moving away at a slow walk. The horse is rendered in Black and Grey Realism while both rider and landscape progressively loosen into Sketch lines making the horse the emotional anchor while the memory surrounding it becomes less literal','A beloved Labrador appears beneath the surface of dark water after retrieving its favorite ball. The face paws and bubbles are rendered in extraordinary Colour Realism while reflections distort parts of the animal naturally. The concept transforms an ordinary behavior the owner remembers into a major piece of art','A deceased Siamese cat is remembered through the exact patch of afternoon sunlight where it slept every day. The cat itself is created mostly from untouched skin inside a warm geometric field of light while only the face paws and tail receive Fine Line definition. The empty surrounding room is implied rather than drawn','A parrots portrait begins in perfect Colour Realism at the head. As the wings open across the shoulder individual feathers progressively transform into Watercolour Illustrative lines Dotwork and finally pure gestural color. Despite the artistic transformation the birds exact natural colors remain the foundation','A man with two dogs has them portrayed running toward him from a distance. One is his current dog and one has passed away. Both animals remain equally solid and alive. The distinction is made only through atmosphere with the older companion moving through softer light while the current dog occupies stronger foreground contrast. Nothing explicitly represents death','Create the ultimate personal pet tattoo from the customers own animal and life with that animal. Use the pets actual face distinctive markings age physical imperfections and expression. Integrate one real object or behavior that uniquely belongs to the relationship such as a collar tag toy blanket favorite sleeping position familiar trail window car ride or place. Choose the tattoo style based on the emotional character of the relationship rather than forcing a predetermined visual language. Allow realism to meet drawing color abstraction negative space or another appropriate style if doing so makes the story stronger. The final artwork must not look like a generic pet portrait surrounded by decorative filler. Someone who knows the animal should immediately know exactly who it is')
$b['A senior Golden Retriever looks directly toward the viewer in soft Black and Grey Realism. The grey muzzle slightly cloudy eyes and uneven fur around the ears are preserved rather than beautified away. The portrait fades naturally into skin below the chest so nothing feels like a photograph pasted onto the body'] = 'Two panels side by side on one image, divided down the middle. LEFT PANEL: the tattoo design alone on a plain white background, shown flat exactly as described, no body, drawn large so it fills most of the panel. RIGHT PANEL: Studio photograph of a real person''s body showing the same exact tattoo where described, healed tattoo on real skin in soft even light, the rest of the body modestly covered by simple plain clothing, only the tattooed area bare, plain seamless light grey studio backdrop - no room, no furniture, no scenery. The tattoo in both panels is identical. The tattoo: A senior Golden Retriever looks directly toward the viewer in soft Black and Grey Realism. The grey muzzle, slightly cloudy eyes and uneven fur around the ears are preserved rather than beautified away. The portrait fades naturally into skin below the chest so nothing feels like a photograph pasted onto the body. Loving, warm, honest. In the right panel it is on a woman, outer upper arm. Create exceptional contemporary tattoo inspiration centered on a specific beloved pet. PETS = WHO I LOVE. The emotional subject is not a generic species. It is one individual animal. The example animal shown in each concept is only an example. NEVER LET THE EXAMPLE PET BECOME THE DESIGN. THE DESIGN MUST STILL WORK WHEN THE CUSTOMER REPLACES THE EXAMPLE WITH THEIR OWN PET. If the concept shows a Doberman, the underlying artistic idea should still work with a Golden Retriever, mixed-breed dog, cat, rabbit, horse, bird or another companion animal whenever logically appropriate. Rotate pets continuously. Do not create a catalog dominated by one or two popular breeds. Include a broad natural mix of dogs, cats, horses, rabbits, birds, reptiles, small mammals and unusual companion animals. Within dogs, rotate breeds, sizes, coat types, ages and appearances. Within cats, rotate coat patterns, breeds, body types and ages. Include mixed-breed animals. Include senior animals. Include young animals. Include rescued animals. Include animals with physical characteristics that make them individually recognizable. Do not beautify away identity. If the real dog has one ear that sits differently, preserve it. If the cat has a torn ear, preserve it. If the senior animal has a grey muzzle, preserve it. If the pet has one eye, preserve it. If the animal has an unusual tooth, scar, coat patch, blaze, feather pattern, scale pattern or posture, preserve it. INDIVIDUALITY IS MORE IMPORTANT THAN BREED PERFECTION. Use the full artistic vocabulary of tattooing. Realism. Black and Grey Realism. Colour Realism. Micro Realism. Fine Line. Sketch. Dotwork. Blackwork. Watercolour. Illustrative. Neo-Traditional. New School. Geometric. Negative Space. Ornamental. Surrealism. And intelligent combinations. Do not rotate styles mechanically. Choose a style because it improves the specific idea. A realistic portrait may be right when exact likeness is the emotional center. Sketch may be right when movement or memory is important. Watercolour may be right when softness or color carries the feeling. Blackwork may be right for a dark animal or powerful silhouette. Fine Line may be right for intimacy and restraint. Dotwork may be right for texture. New School may be right for a pet with enormous personality. Ornamental treatment may be right when the pet is being elevated into something precious. The style serves the relationship. Pet tattoos do not always need the pets face. Explore: Actual paw prints. Actual nose prints. Actual collars. Actual tags. Actual toys. Actual blankets. Actual feathers. Actual horseshoes. Favorite objects. Favorite sleeping positions. Favorite places. Favorite walks. Daily routines. Car rides. Windows. Beds. Chairs. Trails. Hands touching fur. Forehead-to-forehead contact. The way an animal looked back. The way it waited. The way it slept. The way it ran. The way it sat beside someone. The ordinary behavior may contain more emotional truth than a formal portrait. DO NOT USE GENERIC PAW PRINTS WHEN THE CONCEPT CALLS FOR THE CUSTOMERS ACTUAL PAW PRINT. DO NOT USE GENERIC TAGS WHEN THE CUSTOMERS REAL TAG CAN BE USED. DO NOT INVENT PERSONAL DETAILS. The design should invite personalization. Multiple pets must form one composition. Do not default to stacking floating animal heads. Show relationships. Pets can sleep together. Run together. Walk together. Touch noses. Share furniture. Occupy the same environment. Interact naturally. If portrait composition is used, connect the portraits through deliberate structure rather than merely arranging heads vertically. MEMORIAL IS PART OF PETS. MEMORIAL IS NOT ALL OF PETS. Living pets should be celebrated just as strongly. Joy does not require comedy. Show companionship. Energy. Trust. Age. Habit. Comfort. Adventure. Home. Personality. Affection. Memorial concepts should avoid automatic cliches. Do not automatically add: Angel wings. Halos. Heavenly clouds. Generic infinity symbols. Generic heartbeat lines. Generic paw icons. RIP text. Clocks. Dates surrounded by decorative filler. These elements can be used when specifically meaningful to the customer, but death itself does not require a visual symbol. Sometimes the empty collar is enough. Sometimes the sleeping position is enough. Sometimes the old tennis ball is enough. Sometimes the grey muzzle is enough. Sometimes the familiar window is enough. Sometimes the animal simply walking away is enough. Design for the body. Do not place a rectangular photograph on skin. Allow portraits to fade naturally. Allow full bodies to follow anatomy. Allow horses to use long placements. Allow birds to open across shoulders. Allow snakes and long-bodied pets to wrap. Allow sleeping animals to form natural curved compositions. Allow multiple pets enough space to interact. Use small tattoos where intimacy benefits from small scale. Use medium tattoos for most portrait and relationship concepts. Use large scale only when the artistic idea deserves it. Do not make everything a portrait. Do not make everything memorial. Do not make everything sentimental. Do not make everything cute. Do not make everything realistic. Do not make everything Fine Line. Do not make everything a dog. Do not make everything a cat. Do not make everything a Golden Retriever. Do not make everything a Maine Coon. Do not make every animal young and perfect. Do not use generic breed stereotypes as personality. The customers animal provides the personality. THE PET IS NOT A SYMBOL UNTIL THE CUSTOMER MAKES IT ONE. THE PET IS FIRST A RELATIONSHIP. The goal of every inspiration image is for someone to think: THAT IS NOT MY PET. BUT I WANT THAT IDEA WITH MY PET'
